#N canvas 40 60 1280 920 12;
#X declare -path ..;
#X obj 0 0 cnv 1 1280 46 empty empty 03\ \ \ Anatomy\ of\ a\ neuron\ \ -\ \ weights\,\ sum\,\ bias\,\ activation 14 23 0 20 #1d3557 #ffffff 0;
#X obj 1110 890 declare -path ..;
#X text 800 890 finds the nn.* objects one folder up ->, f 42;
#X text 20 890 neuralplay - Moisés Horta Valenzuela / SEMILLA.AI Studio, f 70;
#X text 20 56 Lesson 2 was the curve. Now the whole neuron: several inputs \, each scaled by a WEIGHT \, added up \, shifted by a BIAS and bent by the ACTIVATION. On the left it is built from plain Pd objects \, on the right the same neuron is one [nn.neuron~] box. Link them and compare., f 175;
#X obj 10 96 cnv 1 390 610 empty empty BIOLOGY\ ->\ MATH 8 12 0 13 #eef1f5 #1d3557 0;
#X text 20 122 A real neuron collects signals on its dendrites. Every synapse is stronger or weaker - its WEIGHT - and can excite (positive) or inhibit (negative). The cell body adds everything up and \, if the total is high enough \, the axon fires., f 52;
#X text 20 218 The artificial neuron:, f 52;
#X text 30 239 y = f( w1*x1 + w2*x2 + w3*x3 + b ), f 52;
#X text 20 260 WEIGHT = how much an input matters: a gain knob that can also go negative (phase-inverted). BIAS = the neuron's own tendency: a constant offset added to the sum. f = the activation curve., f 52;
#X text 20 341 So a neuron is a mixing desk followed by a distortion pedal - a NON-LINEAR MIXER. Bending a mix of three oscillators creates combination tones (intermodulation): frequencies that none of the inputs had. Watch the spectrum., f 52;
#X text 20 422 Many neurons with different weights = many different non-linear mixes of the same inputs. That is a layer (lesson 08)., f 52;
#X obj 410 96 cnv 1 430 610 empty empty BUILT\ FROM\ SCRATCH 8 12 0 13 #e3f0fb #1d3557 0;
#X obj 430 134 osc~ 110;
#X obj 520 134 osc~ 137.5;
#X obj 610 134 osc~ 165;
#X text 700 126 <- three inputs x1 x2 x3 (a major chord \, ratios 4:5:6), f 20;
#X obj 430 220 vsl 17 110 -2 2 0 1 \$0-w1 l03-w1 w1 0 -9 0 12 #8ee68e #000000 #000000 7100 1;
#X floatatom 430 338 5 0 0 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 430 364 \$1 20;
#X obj 430 390 line~;
