#X obj 850 716 cnv 1 420 190 empty empty TRY\ THIS 8 12 0 13 #e6f6e9 #1d3557 0;
#X text 860 742 1) Move one fader at a time. Large weights = heavy saturation = many new partials in the spectrum., f 58;
#X text 860 778 2) Pull w2 negative: that input is now inverted (inhibitory). Move the bias: DC and even harmonics., f 58;
#X text 860 814 3) Link off \, then randomize: a random neuron is a random non-linear mixer - the starting point of every neural network., f 58;
